    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "6e71547c3f769f587090f4f57d3809c452454bec27f5e1269ab7668ae8d30d9c",
      "text": "Breakfast. At the scheduled time, meet your English-speaking guide at the hotel and transfer to the station for the train to Aguas Calientes, followed by a guided tour of Machu Picchu. Built by the Inca ruler Pachacútec as a royal estate, with a palace complex, noble residences and temples, the citadel stands at 2,450 metres and was never found by the Spanish conquerors. Brought to international attention in 1911 by the American explorer Hiram Bingham, it still astonishes visitors with its perfectly fitted stonework and resilient buildings in harmony with the landscape.\n\nA UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1983, Machu Picchu was named one of the New Seven Wonders of the World in 2007. In the afternoon, descend to Aguas Calientes for lunch at the El Mapi restaurant, then return by train to Cusco and transfer to the hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1TxH9LDDzR5Bfjb0u_5CBmF_2N5kGi2ad",
